 # storage/ — sole owner of IndexedDB, OPFS, navigator.storage and localStorage (prefs.ts) (spine AD-2); imports model/ only (AD-1).
 
 db.ts `importTakes` (story "Restore from a backup", 6.6) writes whole records as given (writer `restore`, no `updatedAt` stamp) in one transaction, skipping any take id already stored (its record and tab are never overwritten), resolves to the number written and always emits one `library-restored` with that count. restore.ts reads a backup zip through the backup worker's `read` request (backup-worker.ts stays the only importer of fflate) and `validateBackup` checks the manifest and every audio entry in full before anything is written; any unreadable or invalid file is `backup-invalid`.
+
+persistence.ts (story "Storage protection and Library states", 6.7) owns `navigator.storage`: `requestPersistOnce()` (persist() at most once per page load, only when `persisted()` is false; recording-session calls it after a take is saved), `persisted()` (false when the API is missing or throws; waits for a request in flight) and `estimateUsage()` (`estimate().usage`, null when unknown); none throws. It also keeps the storage-full status, with its own `subscribeStorageFull` (not a `StorageEvent`): write-guard.ts `toStorageError` sets it on every `storage-full` result (QuotaExceededError, and the dev hooks), and the next committed save clears it (persistence.ts listens to events.ts for `take-put`, `tab-put` and `library-restored`). It is in memory only: it survives navigation, not a reload. Dev builds: `window.__storageFullSaveHook` (dev/hooks/storage-full.ts) makes `writeCompressed`, `patchTake` and `putTab` reject `storage-full` through `assertDevSaveSpace` until cleared.
